---
argmap-version: 0.3
title: "Semantics audit: undercuts"
description: "Seven questions about what an undercut does under the shipped solve, one declared group each, whole-block copies of the toy battery with suffixed ids: its factor, reinstatement, where a response keeps its ground, a conclusion pinned against the line, the kind key, the shapes, and a refined line undercut from outside. Each head states the question and the measured answer."
---

# GENERATED by mvp/scripts/build-audit.mjs from examples/toys/ - edit the
# toy or the spec, then regenerate; tests/audit.test.ts compares.

::u1 [U1: the undercut as a factor]: The 0.8 line alone brings C to 0.700 from a free A. A 0.7 undercut guarded by a free B lowers it to 0.630, the same undercut with no guard, always in force, to 0.560. With C pinned 0.3 against the line the solve doubts the premise, A 0.399, and leans on the defeat context, B 0.551.

  # u1a: the 0.8 line by itself
  @a-u1a [A]: free
  @c-u1a [C]: derived
  $ev-u1a [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u1a | @a-u1a: the target

  # u1b: a 0.7 undercut guarded by a free statement B
  @a-u1b [A]: free
  @b-u1b [B, the guard]: free
  @c-u1b [C]: derived
  $ev-u1b [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u1b | @a-u1b: the target
  $uc-u1b [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u1b | @b-u1b AND $ev-u1b: the undercut

  # u1c: the same undercut with no guard
  @a-u1c [A]: free
  @c-u1c [C]: derived
  $ev-u1c [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u1c | @a-u1c: the target
  $uc-u1c [the inference fails] 0.7 ~@c-u1c | $ev-u1c: the guardless undercut

  # u1d: the conclusion pinned 0.3 against the line
  @a-u1d [A]: free
  @b-u1d [B, the guard]: free
  @c-u1d [C] 0.3: pinned low against the support
  $ev-u1d [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u1d | @a-u1d: the target
  $uc-u1d [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u1d | @b-u1d AND $ev-u1d: the undercut

::u2 [U2: reinstatement]: The undercut of U1 answered by a response at 0, at 0.6 and at 0.99: C reads 0.630, 0.651, 0.665. A response at 0 is a fact and leaves the undercut whole; at 0.99 it restores nearly all of the line.

  # u2a: the response at 0: the undercut alone
  @a-u2a [A]: free
  @b-u2a [B, the undercut's guard]: free
  @c-u2a [C]: derived
  @d-u2a [D, the response's guard]: free
  $ev-u2a [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u2a | @a-u2a: the target
  $uc-u2a [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u2a | @b-u2a AND $ev-u2a: the undercut
  $resp-u2a [D answers the objection] 0 @c-u2a | @d-u2a AND $uc-u2a: the response, inert

  # u2b: the response at 0.6
  @a-u2b [A]: free
  @b-u2b [B, the undercut's guard]: free
  @c-u2b [C]: derived
  @d-u2b [D, the response's guard]: free
  $ev-u2b [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u2b | @a-u2b: the target
  $uc-u2b [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u2b | @b-u2b AND $ev-u2b: the undercut
  $resp-u2b [D answers the objection] 0.6 @c-u2b | @d-u2b AND $uc-u2b: the response

  # u2c: the response at 0.99
  @a-u2c [A]: free
  @b-u2c [B, the undercut's guard]: free
  @c-u2c [C]: derived
  @d-u2c [D, the response's guard]: free
  $ev-u2c [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u2c | @a-u2c: the target
  $uc-u2c [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u2c | @b-u2c AND $ev-u2c: the undercut
  $resp-u2c [D answers the objection] 0.99 @c-u2c | @d-u2c AND $uc-u2c: the response

::u3 [U3: where a response keeps its ground]: An objection at 0.2 against C, answered by a response at 0.9 whose ground G is pinned 0.85. With the ground inside the response's guard, the flagship shape, C reads 0.488: the answer only revives the worlds the objection killed and delivers nothing of its own. With the ground as its own line beside a guardless response, 0.881. The delivering line alone, the objection unanswered, 0.864. With an independent 0.9 support from a 0.8 root added to each shape, 0.855 against 0.966. The shape of an answer decides more than its strength.

  # u3a: the ground inside the guard (the flagship shape)
  @w-u3a [W, the objection's ground]: free
  @g-u3a [G, the response's ground] 0.85: a pinned root
  @c-u3a [C]: derived
  $obj-u3a [W argues against C] 0.2 ~@c-u3a | @w-u3a: the objection
  $resp-u3a [G answers the objection] 0.9 @c-u3a | @g-u3a AND $obj-u3a: the response, grounds in the guard

  # u3b: the ground as its own line beside a guardless response
  @w-u3b [W, the objection's ground]: free
  @g-u3b [G, the response's ground] 0.85: a pinned root
  @c-u3b [C]: derived
  $obj-u3b [W argues against C] 0.2 ~@c-u3b | @w-u3b: the objection
  $resp-u3b [the objection fails] 0.9 @c-u3b | $obj-u3b: the response, guardless
  $gline-u3b [G supports C] 0.9 @c-u3b | @g-u3b: the grounds as a delivering line

  # u3c: the delivering line alone, the objection unanswered
  @w-u3c [W, the objection's ground]: free
  @g-u3c [G, the response's ground] 0.85: a pinned root
  @c-u3c [C]: derived
  $obj-u3c [W argues against C] 0.2 ~@c-u3c | @w-u3c: the objection
  $gline-u3c [G supports C] 0.9 @c-u3c | @g-u3c: the grounds as a delivering line

  # u3d: the guard shape with an independent 0.9 support
  @s-u3d [S, an independent ground] 0.8: a pinned root
  @w-u3d [W, the objection's ground]: free
  @g-u3d [G, the response's ground] 0.85: a pinned root
  @c-u3d [C]: derived
  $sup-u3d [S supports C] 0.9 @c-u3d | @s-u3d: the independent support
  $obj-u3d [W argues against C] 0.2 ~@c-u3d | @w-u3d: the objection
  $resp-u3d [G answers the objection] 0.9 @c-u3d | @g-u3d AND $obj-u3d: the response, grounds in the guard

  # u3e: the split shape with the same support
  @s-u3e [S, an independent ground] 0.8: a pinned root
  @w-u3e [W, the objection's ground]: free
  @g-u3e [G, the response's ground] 0.85: a pinned root
  @c-u3e [C]: derived
  $sup-u3e [S supports C] 0.9 @c-u3e | @s-u3e: the independent support
  $obj-u3e [W argues against C] 0.2 ~@c-u3e | @w-u3e: the objection
  $resp-u3e [the objection fails] 0.9 @c-u3e | $obj-u3e: the response, guardless
  $gline-u3e [G supports C] 0.9 @c-u3e | @g-u3e: the grounds as a delivering line

::u4 [U4: a conclusion pinned against the line]: A and B at 0.9 and C pinned 0.2 against a 0.8 line and its 0.7 undercut: C holds at 0.202, and it is the undercut that bends, to 0.714, while the line keeps 0.793. Keyed deductive against a hope, the line holds at 0.800 and the undercut takes all of it, 0.744.

  # u4a: A and B at 0.9, C at 0.2 against the line
  @a-u4a [A] 0.9: pinned
  @b-u4a [B, the guard] 0.9: pinned
  @c-u4a [C] 0.2: pinned low against the support
  $ev-u4a [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u4a | @a-u4a: the target
  $uc-u4a [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u4a | @b-u4a AND $ev-u4a: the undercut

  # u4b: the same, the line deductive and the undercut a hope
  @a-u4b [A] 0.9: pinned
  @b-u4b [B, the guard] 0.9: pinned
  @c-u4b [C] 0.2: pinned low against the support
  $ev-u4b [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u4b | @a-u4b: the target  # kind: deductive
  $uc-u4b [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u4b | @b-u4b AND $ev-u4b: the undercut  # kind: hope

::u5 [U5: the kind key on the undercut]: C pinned 0.9 against the undercut, A and B at 0.95: the kind key moves the undercut's solved strength only slightly, 0.695 bare against 0.700 keyed formal, and C reads 0.899 in both. At strength 1 keyed formal the undercut is a fact, 1.000, and C still reads 0.899: the point on C is honoured through the worlds the undercut leaves alive.

  # u5a: no key, the bare count
  @a-u5a [A] 0.95: pinned
  @b-u5a [B, the guard] 0.95: pinned
  @c-u5a [C] 0.9: pinned against the undercut
  $ev-u5a [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u5a | @a-u5a: the target
  $uc-u5a [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u5a | @b-u5a AND $ev-u5a: the undercut, no key

  # u5b: keyed formal, next to hard
  @a-u5b [A] 0.95: pinned
  @b-u5b [B, the guard] 0.95: pinned
  @c-u5b [C] 0.9: pinned against the undercut
  $ev-u5b [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u5b | @a-u5b: the target
  $uc-u5b [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u5b | @b-u5b AND $ev-u5b: the undercut  # kind: formal

  # u5c: keyed formal at strength 1, a fact
  @a-u5c [A] 0.95: pinned
  @b-u5c [B, the guard] 0.95: pinned
  @c-u5c [C] 0.9: pinned against the undercut
  $ev-u5c [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u5c | @a-u5c: the target
  $uc-u5c [B defeats the inference] 1 ~@c-u5c | @b-u5c AND $ev-u5c: the undercut, a fact  # kind: formal

::u6 [U6: the shapes]: Five shapes, each read against its hand formula. Under an undercut of a two-premise line C reads 0.565; of a 0.7/0.2 pair line 0.573, the opposed side untouched; under two undercuts 0.597; under an undercut, a response and a rebuttal of the response 0.650; and an outside objection answered from inside a refinement leaves C at 0.490 with the interior step at 0.882.

  # u6a: the undercut on a two-premise line
  @a-u6a [A]: free
  @x-u6a [X]: free
  @b-u6a [B, the guard]: free
  @c-u6a [C]: derived
  $ev-u6a [A and X support C] 0.8 @c-u6a | @a-u6a AND @x-u6a: the linked target
  $uc-u6a [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u6a | @b-u6a AND $ev-u6a: the undercut

  # u6b: the undercut on a 0.7/0.2 pair line
  @a-u6b [A]: free
  @b-u6b [B, the guard]: free
  @c-u6b [C]: derived
  $ev-u6b [A bears on C both ways] 0.7/0.2 @c-u6b | @a-u6b: the pair line
  $uc-u6b [B defeats the forward inference] 0.6 ~@c-u6b | @b-u6b AND $ev-u6b: the undercut

  # u6c: two undercuts on one line
  @a-u6c [A]: free
  @b-u6c [B, the first guard]: free
  @d-u6c [D, the second guard]: free
  @c-u6c [C]: derived
  $ev-u6c [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u6c | @a-u6c: the target
  $uc1-u6c [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u6c | @b-u6c AND $ev-u6c: the first undercut
  $uc2-u6c [D defeats the inference] 0.5 ~@c-u6c | @d-u6c AND $ev-u6c: the second undercut

  # u6d: undercut, response, rebuttal of the response
  @a-u6d [A]: free
  @b-u6d [B, the undercut's guard]: free
  @d-u6d [D, the response's guard]: free
  @f-u6d [F, the third level's guard]: free
  @c-u6d [C]: derived
  $ev-u6d [A supports C] 0.8 @c-u6d | @a-u6d: the target
  $uc-u6d [B defeats the inference] 0.7 ~@c-u6d | @b-u6d AND $ev-u6d: the undercut
  $resp-u6d [D answers the objection] 0.8 @c-u6d | @d-u6d AND $uc-u6d: the response
  $uc2-u6d [F defeats the response] 0.6 ~@c-u6d | @f-u6d AND $resp-u6d: the third level

  # u6e: an outside objection answered from inside a refinement
  @w-u6e [W, the objection's ground]: free
  @g-u6e [G, the answer's ground] 0.85: a pinned root
  @c-u6e [C]: derived
  $obj-u6e [W argues against C] 0.2 ~@c-u6e | @w-u6e: the outside objection
  $resp-u6e [G answers the objection] 0.9 @c-u6e | @g-u6e AND $obj-u6e: the coarse answer, refined below
    @i-u6e [I, the interior step]: derived
    $iev-u6e [G establishes I] 0.9 @i-u6e | @g-u6e: the interior step
    $fine-u6e [I answers the objection] 0.9 @c-u6e | @i-u6e AND $obj-u6e: the final step, an inhibitor of the outside line

::u7 [U7: a refined line undercut from outside]: A two-step refined line undercut from outside and consumed downstream, beside its hand twin with the steps flat and the undercut re-aimed on the final step, the spine's first step in its guard: the two read the same on every shared statement, C 0.788, D 0.743, the interior step 0.820. What the re-aim rule buys (D51).

  # u7a: the refined line, undercut from outside, consumed downstream
  @a-u7a [A] 0.8: a pinned root
  @b-u7a [B, the undercut's guard]: free
  @c-u7a [C]: derived
  @d-u7a [D, the consumer's conclusion]: derived
  $coarse-u7a [A supports C] 0.7 @c-u7a | @a-u7a: refined below
    @i-u7a [I, the interior step]: derived
    $s1-u7a [A establishes I] 0.8 @i-u7a | @a-u7a: the first step
    $fine-u7a [I supports C] 0.9 @c-u7a | @i-u7a: the final step
  $uc-u7a [B defeats the inference] 0.5 ~@c-u7a | @b-u7a AND $coarse-u7a: the outside undercut of the summary
  $plan-u7a [if the case stands, D] 0.9 @d-u7a | $coarse-u7a: the consumer

  # u7b: the hand twin: the steps flat, the undercut re-aimed on the final step
  @a-u7b [A] 0.8: a pinned root
  @b-u7b [B, the undercut's guard]: free
  @c-u7b [C]: derived
  @d-u7b [D, the consumer's conclusion]: derived
  @i-u7b [I, the interior step]: derived
  $s1-u7b [A establishes I] 0.8 @i-u7b | @a-u7b: the first step
  $fine-u7b [I supports C] 0.9 @c-u7b | @i-u7b: the final step
  $uc-u7b [B defeats the inference] 0.5 ~@c-u7b | @b-u7b AND $s1-u7b AND $fine-u7b: the undercut re-aimed on the final step, the spine conjunct joining its guard (D51 item 2)
  $plan-u7b [if the case stands, D] 0.9 @d-u7b | $fine-u7b AND $s1-u7b: the consumer on the composite by hand
